@bank dept:guest
// Writer (command: guests), batch 3b. Shared lines for guests and visitors (passengers, scientists, couriers, musicians):
// people aboard for a few days. Neutral in personality; voice tokens carry the person. Event guests have their own files.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- {hi}. I'm only aboard a few days. Is it always this friendly?
- {hi}. Sorry, I'm a visitor. Which way is the mess? I keep ending up in the garden.   #funny
- {hi}. You must be crew. The uniform gives it away.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance
- {hi}, {me}. I've nearly learnt the lifts. Just in time to leave.   #funny
? time:morning
- {hi}. Breakfast here is better than on most stations. Don't tell the stations.   #funny

== bye
- {bye}. Thanks for the company.
- {bye}. I'll remember this ship.

== feel
? mood:high
- Lovely ship. Everyone says hello. Even the Chief of the Watch, nearly.   #funny
? mood:low
- Long way from home, and a long way to go. The tea helps.

== near
? deck:3 act:meal
- Your mess is so busy. On my last ship we ate in shifts of three.
? deck:3 act:free
- I didn't expect a garden. It smells like somewhere I used to live.
? deck:2
- Is that the observatory? Am I allowed in? Oh, good.

== chat
- What's it like, living out here? Properly, I mean. Not the brochure.
- I'm off again soon. Tell me one thing I shouldn't miss before I go.

== smalltalk
- Which deck is this again?
- Lovely view from here.
- Is the lift always this slow?   #funny
